    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "7beaf00ee3f90a527cd88d79d469754fc65c11d9b53c8f632eb37b4f95df63c2",
      "text": "Day 2 · Breakfast. Private transfer (driver only) to the airport for your flight to Cusco; on arrival, meeting at the airport and transfer to the hotel. At more than 3,000 metres above sea level, Cusco was once the capital of the Inca Empire and is considered the archaeological and historical heart of South America. According to legend, it was founded by Manco Cápac, the first Inca, who came from the shores of Lake Titicaca.\n\nOptional: guided panoramic tour of Cusco, visiting the Sacsayhuamán fortress, a massive ceremonial and defensive complex built by the Incas in the 15th century with three tiers of cyclopean walls of enormous stone blocks; the rock-carved shrine of Q’enqo, one of the main places of Inca ritual, together with the Puka Pukara fortress and the Tambomachay water temple; and Qorikancha, the legendary “Temple of Gold”, once the most revered sanctuary of the empire, on whose foundations the Spanish built the Santo Domingo Convent. Return to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "16HHnYhZGS6O1KsC1SnpQnIzksIPR2FTL",
        "documentSha256": "8476e1ffdc69c946b8d41f917f4313870e2431eb57545025cfb5e125505e9026",
